      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Covington became the county seat when Newton County was formed in 1821, and the city incorporated in 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://newtonchamber.com/history-tourism-wild-west-heyday-of-covington-ga/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad in 1845 spurred Covington’s growth, turning it into a regional trade hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covington%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During Sherman's March to the Sea in 1864, troops marched through Covington, looting many buildings but sparing several antebellum homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covington%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, Covington hosts the annual Police Department Fuzz Run, a race celebrated as Georgia’s best and drawing visitors from far and wide.",
